# changes (sorcerer evaluates #eq?, #not-eq?, #match?, #not-match?, #any-of?, #not-any-of? and
# nothing else; a pattern using another predicate or directive is removed or rewritten):
#   textobjects.scm: flattened: ecma's patterns, then jsx's (the two `; inherits:` lines removed);
#     no pattern used an unsupported directive.
#   tags.scm: the method, class, function and arrow-function patterns each began
#     `(comment)* @doc .` and ended with #strip! and #select-adjacent! (documentation text, which
#     sorcerer does not read). Rather than lose the definitions, those two directives and the
#     `@doc` comment are removed from each pattern and the definition is kept. The member call
#     `(call_expression function: (member_expression …) arguments: (_) @reference.call)` marks the
#     whole call, not its arguments (`@reference.call` on the call_expression).
